---
import StandardLifecycleNotice from "../../../components/StandardLifecycleNotice.astro";
import StandardPageLayout from "../../../layouts/StandardPageLayout.astro";
import PageToc from "../../../components/PageToc.astro";
import "../../../styles/standards-poster.css";
import "../../../styles/extended.css";
import metadata from "../../../data/standards/hgb/drs06.json";
---

<StandardPageLayout
  code={metadata.code}
  standardType={metadata.framework}
  title={metadata.title}
  subtitle={metadata.nativeTitle}
  framework="hgb"
  status={metadata.status}
>
  <Fragment slot="toc">
    <PageToc
      items={[
        { id: "s1", label: "An honest gap, flagged rather than filled with a guess" },
        { id: "s2", label: "What would resolve this" },
        { id: "s3", label: "Status summary" },
      ]}
    />
  </Fragment>

  <StandardLifecycleNotice
    type="withdrawn"
    explanation="This standard has been withdrawn."
    targetStatus="Not confirmed"
    
    
  />

  <div class="section-header" id="s1"><span class="num">1</span><h2>An honest gap, flagged rather than filled with a guess</h2><span class="line"></span></div>
  <div class="cols-1">
    <div class="card warn">
<div class="ctitle">An honest gap, flagged rather than filled with a guess</div>
<div class="principle">Multiple sources across this research confirmed DRS 6 was withdrawn as part of the same broader DRSC standard-consolidation wave affecting its neighbouring numbers (DRS 1 through roughly DRS 15a). However, none of the sources consulted gave a fully reliable, specific confirmation of DRS 6's own original subject matter or its direct successor. Rather than assert a specific title with more confidence than the research actually supports – a real risk given how easily a plausible-sounding topic could be mistaken for confirmed fact – this entry is presented honestly as an open item.</div>
</div>
  </div>

  <div class="section-header" id="s2"><span class="num">2</span><h2>What would resolve this</h2><span class="line"></span></div>
  <div class="cols-1">
    <div class="card info">
<div class="ctitle">What would resolve this</div>
<div class="principle">A direct query to the DRSC's own official historical standards archive (drsc.de), or the Bundesanzeiger's own withdrawal notice for DRS 6 specifically, would settle this definitively. Given the numbering position – falling between DRS 5 (Risikoberichterstattung, folded into DRS 20) and DRS 7 (Konzerneigenkapital, replaced by DRS 22) – DRS 6 likely addressed a related, similarly early-generation topic from the DRSC's 1998–2005 output, but this remains an inference rather than a confirmed fact.</div>
</div>
  </div>

  <div class="section-header" id="s3"><span class="num">3</span><h2>Status summary</h2><span class="line"></span></div>
  <div class="cols-1">
    <div class="card">
<div class="ctitle">Status summary</div>
<div class="td-table">
<div class="th"><span>Field</span><span>Detail</span></div>
<div class="tr"><span>Original topic</span><span>Not confirmed – flagged honestly rather than guessed</span></div>
<div class="tr"><span>Status</span><span>Withdrawn, per multiple consistent source references</span></div>
<div class="tr"><span>Successor</span><span>Not confirmed</span></div>
<div class="tr"><span>Recommended action</span><span>Verify directly against drsc.de or the Bundesanzeiger archive before relying on this entry for any specific application</span></div>
</div>
</div>
  </div>

</StandardPageLayout>
